.TH SCREENSHOT 1 "2026-09-20" "caveutils" "caveutils Manual"
.SH NAME
screenshot \- take a screenshot on Wayland or X11 with whatever tools the
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B screenshot MODE
.br
.B screenshot -d SECONDS
.br
.B screenshot -n
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B screenshot
.nf
machine has.

  screenshot [-d SECONDS] [-n] [MODE]

MODE is full, screen, area, window or active. Without a MODE you get a
picker (lib/lazytui.sh). The file goes to DIR under a timestamped name,
is copied to the clipboard and announced with a notification; all of
that, the format and the delay are switches at the top of the script,
and each also has an environment override (SCREENSHOT_DIR, ...).

Backends are tried in order and the first one installed wins:
  Wayland  grim (+ slurp to select, + hyprctl or swaymsg + jq for
           windows), else spectacle, gnome-screenshot or flameshot
  X11      maim, scrot or import (+ xdotool for the active window),
           else the same three desktop tools
A mode a backend can't do natively falls back to the closest one that
it can (window -> area), and says so.

To add a MODE: add its name to MODES, its picker text to mode_help(),
and a case for it in capture_grim() / capture_x11(). To add a backend:
write capture_NAME() and add it to pick_backend().

.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B MODE
full, screen (one monitor), area, window or active window
.TP
.B -d SECONDS
wait before capturing
.TP
.B -n
don't copy to the clipboard or notify
